  "outcomes": [
    "Design and implement Python classes using encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism, and justify a composition-versus-inheritance choice.",
    "Write, test, and debug Python programs that use functions and recursion.",
    "Implement stacks, queues, linked lists, binary trees, hash tables, and heaps from first principles, and extend them to balanced and amortized variants.",
    "Analyze the running time of an algorithm using big-O notation, including amortized and average-case analysis, and justify a structure choice by that analysis in writing.",
    "Implement and compare simple and advanced sorting algorithms, and prove the correctness of one.",
    "Apply dynamic programming and greedy strategies to optimization problems, with a written argument for why the greedy choice is correct where applicable.",
    "Represent graphs and apply BFS, DFS, A*, and minimum spanning tree algorithms to reachability, shortest-path, and network design problems.",
    "Benchmark an implementation against a realistic workload and report the result the way a systems engineer would."
